 "notes": "Defects / behaviours of the original kept:\n- EVALUATE WS-MODE has no WHEN OTHER. An unknown or blank mode starts nothing but still sends\n  'STARTS ISSUED'. Fix: add WHEN OTHER with a SEND TEXT such as 'INVALID MODE'.\n- RECEIVE has no RESP/NOHANDLE/HANDLE CONDITION. Terminal input longer than 20 bytes (including the\n  transid) raises LENGERR, which abends the task with AEIV. Fix: add RESP(WS-RESP) to the RECEIVE\n  and test it.\n- The STARTs have no RESP either. Any non-NORMAL condition takes the default action, an abend\n  through task.abendOnCondition. CicsTask.abcodeFor knows INVREQ and LENGERR only. If TRANSIDERR or\n  TERMIDERR ever occurred it would raise IllegalArgumentException instead. I did not invent an abend\n  code for those; GT02 is defined in the CSD per the navigation facts.\n- Mode X: the ABEND at line 58 is ported as task.abend(\"GTAB\"), as rule 14 requires, and the task\n  ends there. The generated abendGtabL58() is kept unchanged but not called from runTask.\n- WS-INLEN is set by RECEIVE but never used afterwards.\n\nAssumptions / facts:\n- START FROM data is passed as the field's bytes in EBCDIC (IBM037), the region's code page.\n  CicsTask documents this for TS items; for START it is my assumption.\n- executeGtstart has no batch step to port (a CICS-only program, no COMMAREA per the interface\n  facts), so it only logs.\n- No fact was contradicted by the source. The field-testing-open sections (calls, cics_tasks,\n  navigation) match lines 34-58.\n- The \"commarea_length\" values in the calls facts are the START FROM LENGTHs, not a COMMAREA.",
